<item>
            <title>[LU-20755] sanity-sec interop issues with 2.16 server</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20755</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;As seen in test results of debug patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/68576&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68576&lt;/a&gt; , running interop testing between &lt;em&gt;master client&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;2.16 server&lt;/em&gt; hits a number of failures in sanity-sec:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;5 45 47 48b 49 64a
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a first pass, it would be good to check if those failures are real bugs, or rather unavoidable problems due to the older server version. In the latter case, adding an interop version check in the tests would be helpful to avoid hitting these failures every time interop tests are triggered.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
