                            <comment id="502326" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:52:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Chakshu Kansal &amp;lt;ckansal@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69287&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69287&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20755&quot; title=&quot;sanity-sec interop issues with 2.16 server&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20755&quot;&gt;LU-20755&lt;/a&gt; tests: fix sanity-sec/5 and sanity-sec/64a for older servers&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 898b31df14508111c42dd70d2b861ea0e5a37720&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="502331" author="JIRAUSER19503" created="Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:40:02 +0000"  >&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_5 was introduced by &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19996&quot; title=&quot;l_getidentity produces improper logs&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19996&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19996&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; utils: Make l_getidentity produce proper errno&quot;, which is not present in the b2_16 branch. As a result, the expected errno is different on b2_16 servers.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_64a, on b2_16, setting the project ID with &lt;b&gt;lfs project -p&lt;/b&gt; requires the projid_set RBAC role now.&lt;br/&gt;
For the master client running against an older 2.16 server, the test must not request the projid_set role. This role is not supported by the older server, so nodemap_modify rejects the entire RBAC value with EINVAL.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Tests 45, 47, 48b, and 49 are showing timeout failures during interop testing with the 2.16 server.&lt;br/&gt;
The failures appear to have some common LNet and bulk I/O errors, including the client being unable to reach the OSS. However, more investigation is needed to confirm whether they share the same root cause and determine the appropriate fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
